blocking":0},"body":"**Description:** As a developer working with HPE GreenLake APIs, I would like to see GitHub Copilot in Visual Studio Code (VS Code) gain knowledge of HPE GreenLake APIs. This enhancement would greatly benefit all HPE GreenLake customers and Partners by allowing them to seamlessly develop against HPE GreenLake services directly within their code editor.\r\n\r\n[developer.greenlake.hpe.com](https://developer.greenlake.hpe.com)\r\n\r\n**Requested Features:**\r\n\r\nAPI Indexing: Integrate HPE GreenLake API documentation from the public-facing site https://developer.greenlake.hpe.com. GitHub Copilot should index relevant endpoints, authentication methods, and usage examples.\r\n\r\nCode Completions: Provide intelligent code completions for HPE GreenLake API methods, reducing development time and ensuring adherence to best practices.\r\n\r\nError Handling: Assist developers in handling errors specific to HPE GreenLake APIs by suggesting relevant error-handling patterns and solutions.\r\n\r\nDocumentation Comments: Generate accurate and context-aware documentation comments for HPE GreenLake API calls, \r\nimproving code readability and maintainability.\r\n\r\nUnit Test Generation: Automatically create unit tests for HPE GreenLake API functions, ensuring robustness and reliability.\r\nCode Refactoring: Suggest improvements and refactorings related to HPE GreenLake API usage, such as optimizing queries or enhancing error handling.\r\n\r\n**Benefits:**\r\n\r\nAccelerated development: Developers can access HPE GreenLake API information directly within their code editor, reducing the need to switch between documentation and code.\r\nConsistent code quality: GitHub Copilot ensures adherence to best practices and consistent coding patterns.\r\nImproved learning experience: New developers ramping up on HPE GreenLake can benefit from contextual guidance and examples.","closed_by":{"login":"dmitrivMS","id":9581278,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1ODEyNzg=","avatar_url":"